  "caption": "Quinn turned 40, and suddenly the same groceries felt heavier and the stairs felt taller. Sabotage? Not quite.\n\nKay explained that muscle mass can dip a few percent per decade from around 40, and strength often drops even faster. The good news: muscle responds to training at any age.\n\nWhat can help: resistance training about three times a week and kept up long-term, sit-to-stands and squats, daily one-leg balance practice, and protein with each meal (ask your GP or a dietitian what suits you).\n\nGet it checked if you notice unexplained weight loss, poor appetite, sudden or worsening weakness, repeated falls, or fever.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
